/* BALANCE MUST BE RE-READ ON EVERY BLOCK, not only on NEWBALANCE.
   `unconfirmed` in the node's `balance` reply is not a property of the coin — it is purely
   `tip - coin.blockCreated < confirmations` (balance.java:184-195, default depth 3). A coin
   therefore becomes confirmed simply by the chain moving on, and NOTHING is emitted when that
   happens: core posts NEWBALANCE only when a relevant coin is created or spent
   (TxPoWTreeNode.java:309 `if(balancechange)`). Listening for NEWBALANCE alone froze the card on
   the snapshot taken the moment a trade's proceeds arrived — reporting them unconfirmed
   indefinitely, long after they had settled and become spendable. Native polls on NEWBLOCK as
   well (MainActivity:221), as does pandapools-mds; we did not. */
/* Dexicon owns MDS.init (ui/app.js). The PandaDEX page logic is driven through these hooks. */
